ull` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks r