{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794541076553,"sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2fbbe5d0017Qwk5uT4GCObtJ","sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","messageID":"msg_1d2fba0ea001FW6D8mHXF5EYLz","type":"tool","id":"call_5f499f17932042a7aee66e5c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '540,640p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts"},"output":"    ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(top.skill)\n      ? doctorCommandString(top.skill)\n      : sanitizeSkillLabel(metadataSkillLabel(result) ?? top.skill));\n  if (!topLabel) {\n    observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const companion = isDoctorBridgeId(top.skill)\n    ? undefined\n    : recommendations.slice(1).find((recommendation) => doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill) !== null);\n  const companionLabel = companion ? companionCommandLabel(companion.skill, childSession) : null;\n  const companionLine = (shownSecond: string | undefined): string => (\n    companionLabel && companion && companion.skill !== shownSecond ? `\\nAlso: ${companionLabel}` : ''\n  );\n  const capWithCompanion = (head: string, companionText: string, cap: number): string => {\n    const companionFits = head.length + companionText.length <= cap * TOKEN_TO_CHAR_ESTIMATE;\n    return `${capText(head, cap)}${companionFits ? companionText : ''}`;\n  };\n\n  const precomputedAmbiguous = typeof result.ambiguous === 'boolean' ? result.ambiguous : undefined;\n  if (tokenCap > DEFAULT_TOKEN_CAP && second && hasAdvisorAmbiguitySignal(recommendations, precomputedAmbiguous)) {\n    // The scorer names its own tie partners, which can sit below the second passing\n    // entry, so prefer a named partner and fall back to the second entry.\n    const namedPartners = (top as RenderableRecommendation).ambiguousWith;\n    const ambiguousWith: readonly string[] = Array.isArray(namedPartners) ? namedPartners : [];\n    const vs = (ambiguousWith.length > 0\n      ? recommendations.find((recommendation) => ambiguousWith.includes(recommendation.skill))\n      : undefined) ?? second;\n    const vsLabel = recommendationLabel(vs, childSession);\n    if (!vsLabel && !isDoctorBridgeId(vs.skill)) {\n      observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n      return null;\n    }\n    if (vsLabel) {\n      const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; ambiguous: ${topLabel} `\n        + `${formatScore(top.confidence)}/${formatScore(top.uncertainty)} vs ${vsLabel} `\n        + `${formatScore(vs.confidence)}/${formatScore(vs.uncertainty)} pass.`;\n      const rendered = capWithCompanion(\n        head,\n        companionLine(vs.skill),\n        Math.min(tokenCap, AMBIGUOUS_TOKEN_CAP),\n      ) + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n      observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n      return rendered;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; use ${topLabel} `\n    + `${formatScore(top.confidence)}/${formatScore(top.uncertainty)} pass.`;\n  const rendered = capWithCompanion(\n    head,\n    companionLine(undefined),\n    Math.min(tokenCap, DEFAULT_TOKEN_CAP),\n  ) + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n  observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n  return rendered;\n}\n\n/** Classify a result with no brief; no result at all means the advisor did not answer. */\nexport function advisorFallbackCase(\n  result?: Pick<AdvisorHookResult, 'status' | 'freshness'>,\n): AdvisorFallbackClassification {\n  if (!result || result.status === 'fail_open' || result.freshness === 'absent'\n    || (result.freshness === 'unavailable' && result.status !== 'skipped')) {\n    return {\n      fallbackCase: 'outage',\n      outageLabel: result?.freshness === 'absent'\n        ? 'absent'\n        : result?.status === 'degraded'\n          ? 'degraded'\n          : 'fail_open',\n    };\n  }\n  if (result.status === 'skipped' && result.freshness === 'unavailable') {\n    return { fallbackCase: 'skipped' };\n  }\n  return { fallbackCase: 'no-match' };\n}\n\n/** Render the fallback status and directive block when no advisor brief is available. */\nexport function renderAdvisorFallbackDirective(\n  options: AdvisorBriefRenderOptions = {},\n  result?: Pick<AdvisorHookResult, 'status' | 'freshness'>,\n): string {\n  const classification = advisorFallbackCase(result);\n  const head = classification.fallbackCase === 'outage'\n    ? `Advisor: outage (${classification.outageLabel});${options.setupWording === true ? ' for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;' : ''} route by hand: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<request>\"}' --format json`\n    : classification.fallbackCase === 'skipped'\n      ? 'Advisor: prompt skipped.'\n      : options.setupWording === true\n        ? `Advisor: no skill matched.${SETUP_HINT}`\n        : 'Advisor: no skill matched.';\n  const rendered = head + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n  observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n  return rendered;\n}\n\n/** Render the outage fallback used when advisor execution times out or is unavailable. */\nexport function renderAdvisorTimeoutFallback(\n  options: AdvisorBriefRenderOptions = {},\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(top.skill)\n      ? doctorCommandString(top.skill)\n      : sanitizeSkillLabel(metadataSkillLabel(result) ?? top.skill));\n  if (!topLabel) {\n    observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const companion = isDoctorBridgeId(top.skill)\n    ? undefined\n    : recommendations.slice(1).find((recommendation) => doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill) !== null);\n  const companionLabel = companion ? companionCommandLabel(companion.skill, childSession) : null;\n  const companionLine = (shownSecond: string | undefined): string => (\n    companionLabel && companion && companion.skill !== shownSecond ? `\\nAlso: ${companionLabel}` : ''\n  );\n  const capWithCompanion = (head: string, companionText: string, cap: number): string => {\n    const companionFits = head.length + companionText.length <= cap * TOKEN_TO_CHAR_ESTIMATE;\n    return `${capText(head, cap)}${companionFits ? companionText : ''}`;\n  };\n\n  const precomputedAmbiguous = typeof result.ambiguous === 'boolean' ? result.ambiguous : undefined;\n  if (tokenCap > DEFAULT_TOKEN_CAP && second && hasAdvisorAmbiguitySignal(recommendations, precomputedAmbiguous)) {\n    // The scorer names its own tie partners, which can sit below the second passing\n    // entry, so prefer a named partner and fall back to the second entry.\n    const namedPartners = (top as RenderableRecommendation).ambiguousWith;\n    const ambiguousWith: readonly string[] = Array.isArray(namedPartners) ? namedPartners : [];\n    const vs = (ambiguousWith.length > 0\n      ? recommendations.find((recommendation) => ambiguousWith.includes(recommendation.skill))\n      : undefined) ?? second;\n    const vsLabel = recommendationLabel(vs, childSession);\n    if (!vsLabel && !isDoctorBridgeId(vs.skill)) {\n      observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n      return null;\n    }\n    if (vsLabel) {\n      const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; ambiguous: ${topLabel} `\n        + `${formatScore(top.confidence)}/${formatScore(top.uncertainty)} vs ${vsLabel} `\n        + `${formatScore(vs.confidence)}/${formatScore(vs.uncertainty)} pass.`;\n      const rendered = capWithCompanion(\n        head,\n        companionLine(vs.skill),\n        Math.min(tokenCap, AMBIGUOUS_TOKEN_CAP),\n      ) + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n      observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n      return rendered;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; use ${topLabel} `\n    + `${formatScore(top.confidence)}/${formatScore(top.uncertainty)} pass.`;\n  const rendered = capWithCompanion(\n    head,\n    companionLine(undefined),\n    Math.min(tokenCap, DEFAULT_TOKEN_CAP),\n  ) + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n  observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n  return rendered;\n}\n\n/** Classify a result with no brief; no result at all means the advisor did not answer. */\nexport function advisorFallbackCase(\n  result?: Pick<AdvisorHookResult, 'status' | 'freshness'>,\n): AdvisorFallbackClassification {\n  if (!result || result.status === 'fail_open' || result.freshness === 'absent'\n    || (result.freshness === 'unavailable' && result.status !== 'skipped')) {\n    return {\n      fallbackCase: 'outage',\n      outageLabel: result?.freshness === 'absent'\n        ? 'absent'\n        : result?.status === 'degraded'\n          ? 'degraded'\n          : 'fail_open',\n    };\n  }\n  if (result.status === 'skipped' && result.freshness === 'unavailable') {\n    return { fallbackCase: 'skipped' };\n  }\n  return { fallbackCase: 'no-match' };\n}\n\n/** Render the fallback status and directive block when no advisor brief is available. */\nexport function renderAdvisorFallbackDirective(\n  options: AdvisorBriefRenderOptions = {},\n  result?: Pick<AdvisorHookResult, 'status' | 'freshness'>,\n): string {\n  const classification = advisorFallbackCase(result);\n  const head = classification.fallbackCase === 'outage'\n    ? `Advisor: outage (${classification.outageLabel});${options.setupWording === true ? ' for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;' : ''} route by hand: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<request>\"}' --format json`\n    : classification.fallbackCase === 'skipped'\n      ? 'Advisor: prompt skipped.'\n      : options.setupWording === true\n        ? `Advisor: no skill matched.${SETUP_HINT}`\n        : 'Advisor: no skill matched.';\n  const rendered = head + DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE;\n  observeAdvisorPolicy(rendered, options);\n  return rendered;\n}\n\n/** Render the outage fallback used when advisor execution times out or is unavailable. */\nexport function renderAdvisorTimeoutFallback(\n  options: AdvisorBriefRenderOptions = {},\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '540,640p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794541076061,"end":1794541076553}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794541076559,"sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2fbbbc3001cJozcCsjcvTUCl","sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","messageID":"msg_1d2fba0ea001FW6D8mHXF5EYLz","type":"tool","id":"call_8c1080d0973446a4bee3b2ae","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '/^- \\[.\\] T012 /,/^- \\[.\\] T014 /p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md"},"output":"- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '/^- \\\\[.\\\\] T012 /,/^- \\\\[.\\\\] T014 /p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794541075395,"end":1794541076559}}}}
