{"type":"text","timestamp":1794541513793,"sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","part":{"id":"prt_1d3025b7b001kBOYO1S9OaXKNx","sessionID":"ses_e2d068ceaffe9O3kC6bqSOeD4D","messageID":"msg_1d3025632001sl9SE8DfRapGo3","type":"text","text":"T020 complete.\n\n**Files written**\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/typed-heads.mjs`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/typed-heads.json`\n\n`typed-heads.mjs` reads `CORPUS`, keeps `row_type` `typed` with `split` `none`, creates one `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))` sandbox, pipes each row's T006-shaped payload (session id `typed-<id>`) into `$HOOK`, parses the first line of `additionalContext` with `parseOffer` from `OF`, writes the six fields per row, sorts by id, and stops/removes the sandbox. `typed-heads.json` has 44 rows and exactly the keys `id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees`.\n\n**Verify output**\n```\n$ jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json\n44\n$ jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json\ncmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01\n$ ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null\nls exit=1\n```\n\n`node --check` on the script also exits 0. No checkbox in `tasks.md` was touched.\n\n**Two implementation notes**\n- The hook inherited `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` from this worker environment, which made the renderer replace `start`/`ask` with `parent-named only`. The script deletes that variable for the child hook so the measurement sees a reader session.\n- A daemon from another run already held the shared advisor DB lease, so a socket-only sandbox could not start (the launcher bridged and exited, leaving the sandbox socket absent). The script therefore also points `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` inside the same `ssa-typed-*` directory, giving its daemon an isolated lease. Cleanup matches the sandbox directory in a process's command line or environment, since the daemon takes paths from the environment.","time":{"start":1794541509499,"end":1794541513793}}}
